I just finished the first version of my little test side project, called BotApp.  It's a Battlebots-style robot fighting game, using OpenGL for graphics and Bullet for physics and collision detection.  Try it out, let me know what you think of it, how it runs, any bugs, etc.<br><br>Download:  <a href="http://www.tomduggan.net/download/botapp0_1.zip" class="postlink">http://www.tomduggan.net/download/botapp0_1.zip</a> (7.6 mb)<br><br>Some screenshots:<br><img src="http://www.tomduggan.net/images/botapp3_thumb.jpg" class="postimage" alt="Image"><br><br><img src="http://www.tomduggan.net/images/botapp2_thumb.jpg" class="postimage" alt="Image"><br><br><img src="http://www.tomduggan.net/images/botapp1_thumb.jpg" class="postimage" alt="Image"><br><br>For more information and a lot more screenshots, there's a page on my portfolio dedicated to botapp:  <a href="http://www.tomduggan.net" class="postlink">http://www.tomduggan.net</a><br><br>Thanks!<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=5269">TomDuggan</a> — Fri Jun 12, 2009 1:14 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
